    "created_at": "2026-11-24T13:19:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-24T13:19:04Z",
    "body": "Proposal for a change before D1 starts: step the project-file version when a non-sharp tip (flat tip or ball tip) is written.\n\nReason: an older CamCraft that opens such a `.camproj` reads the tip as sharp. A sharp tip is a smaller tool than the real tool. The older build has no door that refuses it. A toolpath that it plans can gouge.\n\nThe issue text says \"no version step\". We ask the maintainer to confirm or refuse this change before D1 starts. Our recommendation: step the version for the tip form only. A sharp taper keeps its file version.\n\nThe `.camtools` library file steps its version for the same reason, as the plan for #3663 says. This follows the `HOLDER_REF_VERSION` precedent.\n\nPlan: the implementation plan in the #3663 comment (PR D1).\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
